  "question": {
    "text": "The earth is moving towards a fixed star with a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>km&#160;s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. An observer on the earth observes a shift of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.58</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#197;</mi></math> in the wavelength of light coming from the star. What is the actual wavelength of light (in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mtext>m</mtext></math> ) emitted by the star?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0.58",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></math><br />Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>km&#160;s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>m&#160;s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>m&#160;s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.58</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m</mtext></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mtext>&#8195;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0.58</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0.58</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0.58</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mtext>m</mtext></math>",
